1
00:00:03,323 --> 00:01:55,356
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:08,833
No living creature was hurt during
the production of this show.

3
00:03:19,150 --> 00:03:23,150
I've been waiting for this.

4
00:03:24,012 --> 00:03:28,012
Don't hold yourself back, Bala Hatun.

5
00:04:09,367 --> 00:04:12,637
It was a good move.

6
00:04:12,637 --> 00:04:15,827
You took it well.

7
00:04:26,802 --> 00:04:30,802
You are going to kill me, huh?

8
00:04:42,949 --> 00:04:47,559
Didn't you tell me to not
hold myself back, Osman Bey?

9
00:04:49,466 --> 00:04:54,396
Come on. Make your move.

10
00:05:14,341 --> 00:05:18,341
Why would someone with
eyes like this...

11
00:05:18,911 --> 00:05:22,911
...need a sword to kill.

12
00:05:24,159 --> 00:05:29,359
These eyes aren't a weapon,
they are a shield, Osman Bey.

13
00:05:30,989 --> 00:05:35,319
They protect me from the tyranny
of your eyes.

14
00:06:29,401 --> 00:06:34,091
It's Aksu Hatun. I met her at
food house.

15
00:06:34,554 --> 00:06:40,814
She is kind, talented and she
helped me a lot.

16
00:06:48,357 --> 00:06:51,937
Thank you, Aksu sister!

17
00:07:09,482 --> 00:07:13,222
Your sherbet is as good
as your name.

18
00:07:14,966 --> 00:07:18,586
Her attitude is also good,
as her face.

19
00:07:18,586 --> 00:07:22,586
Mashallah. Mashallah.

20
00:07:24,119 --> 00:07:29,329
-Who is your husband? Do we know him?
-I don't have a husband yet, Osman Bey.

21
00:07:34,133 --> 00:07:39,013
If not, then, it's your responsibility,
Bala.

22
00:07:40,331 --> 00:07:45,311
Find a good husband for Aksu sister.

23
00:08:19,170 --> 00:08:24,000
-Salam Alaikum, Osman Bey.
-Alaikum Salam, Abdurrahman Ghazi.

24
00:08:24,092 --> 00:08:28,462
Sheikh Edebali sent news.
He is coming.

25
00:08:28,646 --> 00:08:31,566
Thank Allah.

26
00:08:33,140 --> 00:08:35,920
Osman Bey.

27
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:40,830
Targun Hatun is the new leader
of Cumans.

28
00:08:41,886 --> 00:08:46,756
Our child Göktuğ is her right hand.

29
00:08:47,297 --> 00:08:51,297
Mashallah.

30
00:08:51,936 --> 00:08:57,636
I knew he would do it. He is a valiant.

31
00:08:58,287 --> 00:09:02,287
He had been through many troubles for me.

32
00:09:03,450 --> 00:09:07,450
Thank Allah.

33
00:09:23,083 --> 00:09:29,123
So, you and Göktuğ will
take revenge from Osman?

34
00:09:29,713 --> 00:09:33,713
He will pay with his life.

35
00:09:33,713 --> 00:09:38,773
You falsely changed your religion.
Aren't you afraid of committing a sin?

36
00:09:39,143 --> 00:09:42,813
I'll burn in hell for you, Osman Bey.

37
00:09:42,813 --> 00:09:48,153
You'll die in hell for me, huh?
But I live in heaven.

38
00:09:48,865 --> 00:09:52,485
I live with an angel...

39
00:09:52,485 --> 00:09:56,865
...who imprisoned me in her eyes.
-I wish I saved some of that poison...

40
00:09:56,865 --> 00:10:00,865
...and didn't run with a cure.

41
00:10:01,749 --> 00:10:06,279
Because of what you have done to
me and my wife, you are banished!

42
00:10:06,279 --> 00:10:10,829
And about you, Göktuğ,
you failed me.

43
00:10:10,829 --> 00:10:15,759
You couldn't guard my enemy!
You are banished!

44
00:10:16,219 --> 00:10:21,309
Because of a single mistake I've done,
you are forgetting what my brother and I did.

45
00:10:21,309 --> 00:10:24,629
That's what I would expect from a man...

46
00:10:24,629 --> 00:10:28,159
...who banishes the woman who
will burn in hell for him.

47
00:10:32,219 --> 00:10:37,339
Do you think that you can beat Osman?

48
00:10:40,251 --> 00:10:45,401
-Without Rome, you are nothing.
-Göktuğ!

49
00:10:50,025 --> 00:10:55,035
If you want to take revenge,
you have to survive.

50
00:10:55,499 --> 00:11:00,319
So, you need our support.
Our soldiers.

51
00:11:01,312 --> 00:11:03,532
Our gold.

52
00:11:05,484 --> 00:11:10,784
That's what you are after.
That's how you buy victory.

53
00:11:14,127 --> 00:11:19,077
You'll give gold. I'll give soldiers.

54
00:11:19,077 --> 00:11:23,907
Soldiers, huh?
Only soldiers?

55
00:11:25,197 --> 00:11:29,197
I promise you soldier and support.

56
00:11:29,197 --> 00:11:33,197
You should be giving me more than
soldiers.

57
00:11:39,392 --> 00:11:43,392
We'll give you Osman's head.

58
00:11:51,248 --> 00:11:55,968
You convinced me.
If you are so confident...

59
00:11:57,098 --> 00:12:00,978
...let's see if you will convince Nikola.
-Targun, come with me.

60
00:12:00,978 --> 00:12:04,088
We are going to Nikola.

61
00:12:06,111 --> 00:12:11,001
-Göktuğ, you stay here.
-Göktuğ.

62
00:12:11,001 --> 00:12:16,091
Stay with my man. If something happens
to me, you know what to do.

63
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:31,346
Targun Hatun's men want gold for loyalty.

64
00:12:31,764 --> 00:12:35,944
Nikol wants men to fight with us.

65
00:12:36,292 --> 00:12:41,142
For this reason, sooner or later,
they'll come together.

66
00:12:41,142 --> 00:12:46,192
But I'm already ready.

67
00:12:46,378 --> 00:12:49,608
What do you want to do, Osman Bey?

68
00:12:49,608 --> 00:12:54,748
I will outplay you on their plot
with Targun Hatun.

69
00:12:55,494 --> 00:12:58,134
Thank Allah.

70
00:12:58,293 --> 00:13:03,093
Brother, talk to the lord of Koyunhisar,
Yorgo.

71
00:13:03,093 --> 00:13:07,093
But tell me that I want to see
him in secret.

72
00:13:07,287 --> 00:13:13,497
-What's on your mind, Osman Bey?
-He dreamed of being the lord of İnegöl.

73
00:13:13,680 --> 00:13:18,350
But now he is getting his orders
from Nikola.

74
00:13:18,350 --> 00:13:24,190
This is hurting his ego.
We'll give him the opportunity.

75
00:13:25,266 --> 00:13:29,266
We'll take advantage of that.

76
00:13:29,692 --> 00:13:33,692
Nikola will be enemies with all lords.

77
00:13:34,349 --> 00:13:39,429
-All right, Osman Bey. All right.
-Nikola wants us to have more enemies.

78
00:13:40,693 --> 00:13:44,693
He worked with the Mongols against us.

79
00:13:45,754 --> 00:13:49,754
He wanted to sway Yavlak Arslan.

80
00:13:49,973 --> 00:13:55,173
Now the Cumans. We don't know
who is next.

81
00:13:55,491 --> 00:13:59,491
We'll prevent that.

82
00:13:59,491 --> 00:14:03,491
I can't wait to take revenge
for my son.

83
00:14:03,867 --> 00:14:06,837
But you are right, Osman Bey.

84
00:14:08,546 --> 00:14:13,416
We should do what he does.
Give him more enemies.

85
00:14:18,498 --> 00:14:23,798
Trade should go on.
Trade routes should always be open.

86
00:14:23,798 --> 00:14:27,798
Süleyman and Melik Beys caravans
should be protected.

87
00:14:28,112 --> 00:14:34,242
As soon as they enter our lands,
they are our responsibility.

88
00:14:35,581 --> 00:14:40,421
With the gold we get from them,
we'll help the poor.

89
00:14:41,239 --> 00:14:45,869
We'll support tribes that want to
run away from the Mongols.

90
00:14:46,970 --> 00:14:52,170
May Allah help you, Osman Bey.

91
00:14:52,170 --> 00:14:56,170
Amin, amin, Bamsı Bey.
Amin.

92
00:15:05,506 --> 00:15:09,506
I'll lose my head if we fail.

93
00:15:09,506 --> 00:15:13,506
Not only me, Hazal Hatun too.

94
00:15:13,506 --> 00:15:18,566
Dündar Bey, if you do everything
I say...

95
00:15:18,566 --> 00:15:23,306
...no one will even bleed.
Only Osman's reputation.

96
00:15:23,306 --> 00:15:28,576
When he loses his fur,
you will ascend.

97
00:15:31,918 --> 00:15:36,568
Think of everyone who
tried to play me!

98
00:15:36,568 --> 00:15:42,498
Now, those who don't want the
same fate should watch their moves!

99
00:15:45,414 --> 00:15:51,404
If this is like the others,
Osman won't stop.

100
00:15:51,404 --> 00:15:55,604
He will kill me and
you will be in line.

101
00:15:55,604 --> 00:15:59,944
Dündar Bey, no one will know that
it was you!

102
00:15:59,944 --> 00:16:03,454
You will be clueless when we enter
the tents.

103
00:16:03,454 --> 00:16:08,974
You are talking about entering
Kayı Tribe, Nikola. What about the tent?

104
00:16:09,844 --> 00:16:14,484
You, Dündar Bey. You will
take us to the tent.

105
00:16:14,484 --> 00:16:18,484
Me?

106
00:16:18,484 --> 00:16:21,854
Then I'll get out of it
like nothing happened?

107
00:16:21,854 --> 00:16:27,844
Dündar Bey, aren't you a Kayı bey?
Where is your courage?

108
00:16:30,053 --> 00:16:34,883
Have you ever betrayed your emperor?

109
00:16:37,219 --> 00:16:44,439
Until you dare to do that, don't you ever
call me a coward. Ever.

110
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:56,920
All right, Dündar Bey.
You have the right to be afraid.

111
00:16:56,920 --> 00:17:01,990
Then, do you know what will happen?
You'll wait for him to die naturally.

112
00:17:01,990 --> 00:17:05,990
If you have the time and the patience.

113
00:17:05,990 --> 00:17:10,840
I don't have the time or the patience,
Dündar Bey.

114
00:17:12,859 --> 00:17:16,859
If I defeat Osman, Dündar Bey.

115
00:17:16,859 --> 00:17:20,859
Then, I won't need you.

116
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:38,850
All the tribes that ran away from
Mongols, spread to Anatolia.

117
00:17:38,850 --> 00:17:46,380
Dodurga Tribe is around Bolu,
Çorum and Ankara.

118
00:17:47,140 --> 00:17:53,120
Salur Tribe is around Karaman,
Teke and Candaroğlu lands.

119
00:17:53,646 --> 00:18:00,196
Bayat Tribe is around Karahisar,
Çorum and Bolu.

120
00:18:01,440 --> 00:18:08,170
The bravest of them want to
go further from their borders.

121
00:18:08,170 --> 00:18:12,760
They want jihad,
they want battle, Bamsı Bey.

122
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:17,000
I know. Ertuğrul Bey
wrote it all...

123
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:20,460
...on these documents.

124
00:18:20,460 --> 00:18:26,690
We should unite them as once
before they fade out.

125
00:18:27,117 --> 00:18:31,117
We should help them...

126
00:18:31,117 --> 00:18:35,117
...we should give them
lands and tents.

127
00:18:35,401 --> 00:18:39,701
The heathens have lands.

128
00:18:39,701 --> 00:18:44,288
If we kick their lords from there,
we'll locate the tribes.

129
00:18:44,723 --> 00:18:48,723
That's what we will do, Bamsı Bey.
Then, we should invite them.

130
00:18:48,723 --> 00:18:53,053
We should give them the conquered
lands.

131
00:18:53,053 --> 00:18:59,053
They'll join us as they hear it.
And it will be Turkmen tribes everywhere.

132
00:18:59,647 --> 00:19:05,227
-We'll grow even stronger, Bamsı Bey.
-Then, Osman Bey...

133
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:09,227
...we'll have an army.
-We'll have an army.

134
00:19:09,227 --> 00:19:16,237
And everyone will unite under our banner.
We'll chase the heathens to Constantinople!

135
00:19:16,841 --> 00:19:20,841
Now is the time to go to...

136
00:19:20,841 --> 00:19:24,841
...the tribes of those valiants,
one by one, and invite them.

137
00:19:24,841 --> 00:19:30,111
All right, Osman Be.y
All right.

138
00:19:36,157 --> 00:19:42,147
You will bring Bamsı Bey from
this way.

139
00:19:42,333 --> 00:19:47,803
Germiyan path. There aren't
many guards there.

140
00:19:48,122 --> 00:19:52,122
They'll wait for you there.
Bring Bamsı alone...

141
00:19:52,967 --> 00:19:56,557
...so that he won't create
a problem.

142
00:19:56,557 --> 00:20:01,277
He is scared like a little child that
Osman will take his sword.

143
00:20:01,527 --> 00:20:05,527
He told me to not tell anyone
about his injury.

144
00:20:05,695 --> 00:20:09,516
This will be very easy.

145
00:20:09,516 --> 00:20:13,986
When Bamsı leaves the tents...

146
00:20:13,986 --> 00:20:17,986
...we'll have all the documents.

147
00:20:20,146 --> 00:20:26,686
-What about the caravan?
-Flatyos will bring us the caravan.

148
00:20:27,703 --> 00:20:33,223
Finally, I will give the document to
the Pope.

149
00:20:33,223 --> 00:20:38,023
Three days later, a ship will take
off from the harbor.

150
00:20:38,357 --> 00:20:44,957
And when this is done, you'll kiss
his ring proudly, David.

151
00:20:45,241 --> 00:20:49,241
And for living with these
barbarians for years...

152
00:20:49,241 --> 00:20:53,241
...you will be awarded.

153
00:20:53,241 --> 00:20:57,891
The greatest award is the heaven
of Jesus Christ.

154
00:21:02,769 --> 00:21:08,809
He sighed deeply and said,

155
00:21:08,809 --> 00:21:12,809
“Why does this generation ask for a sign?

156
00:21:12,809 --> 00:21:16,809
Truly I tell you, no sign will
be given to it.”

157
00:21:17,349 --> 00:21:22,769
Then he left them,
got back into the boat...

158
00:21:23,544 --> 00:21:29,094
...and crossed to the other side.

159
00:21:40,058 --> 00:21:44,058
You will tell me what happened
in that castle, Lena!

160
00:21:44,306 --> 00:21:48,306
Bayhoca said that Flatyos
took you to the dungeon.

161
00:21:48,306 --> 00:21:51,656
Don't tell me that it
was a courtesy!

162
00:21:55,618 --> 00:22:00,448
I knew Flatyos from Karacahisar.

163
00:22:01,199 --> 00:22:06,739
I knew that he loved me before
I met you.

164
00:22:17,427 --> 00:22:22,447
Savcı, I hid this from you...

165
00:22:22,568 --> 00:22:28,958
...because I was afraid that
your rage could hurt you.

166
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:35,580
So, I didn't tell you.

167
00:22:36,760 --> 00:22:41,710
What happened in that castle, Lena?
What happened in that castle?

168
00:22:46,420 --> 00:22:53,390
I begged Flatyos to let
our child go.

169
00:22:53,630 --> 00:22:57,630
So, you begged him?

170
00:22:59,774 --> 00:23:04,884
I've done what a mother in
pain should do, Savcı.

171
00:23:07,605 --> 00:23:11,605
I had hemlock poison with me...

172
00:23:12,083 --> 00:23:16,083
...I was going to save my son
and kill myself.

173
00:23:18,028 --> 00:23:22,028
I wouldn't let them pollute
your honor.

174
00:23:54,758 --> 00:23:59,308
Everyone deserves a second chance, Targun.

175
00:23:59,308 --> 00:24:03,308
If what you say is right,
it will be a good use for me.

176
00:24:03,308 --> 00:24:08,788
If not, then I'll kill you.

177
00:24:09,141 --> 00:24:13,141
By the way, Osman's man, Göktuğ...

178
00:24:13,141 --> 00:24:17,141
...what is he doing with you.

179
00:24:17,141 --> 00:24:21,141
I owe him. He killed my father's killer
with me.

180
00:24:21,629 --> 00:24:27,249
Without Göktuğ, I wouldn't
be leading the Cumans.

181
00:24:28,611 --> 00:24:33,811
So, how will I know that he isn't
Osman's spy.

182
00:24:33,811 --> 00:24:38,161
Just give him a chance. I'll send him
to the caravan with Flatyos.

183
00:24:38,161 --> 00:24:42,781
You will use him like me.
When we get our revenge...

184
00:24:42,781 --> 00:24:48,921
...maybe we'll remember our old
enmities, Nikola.

185
00:24:52,036 --> 00:24:56,036
Don't doubt that, Targun.

186
00:24:56,036 --> 00:25:00,036
So, we'll do this.

187
00:25:00,036 --> 00:25:04,036
Flatyos and Göktuğ will raid the
caravan.

188
00:25:04,036 --> 00:25:09,896
You will go to Söğüt and kill Bala
who has been in the food house lately.

189
00:25:11,387 --> 00:25:17,577
So, we'll see how you and Göktuğ
keep your promises.

190
00:25:17,577 --> 00:25:21,577
-Did you like that?
-Killing Bala?

191
00:25:22,017 --> 00:25:25,077
Is that what you want?

192
00:25:25,603 --> 00:25:30,433
I thought you would like that.
Am I wrong.

193
00:25:32,426 --> 00:25:37,516
Nothing can make me feel that good.

194
00:25:38,874 --> 00:25:43,954
Good. Then everyone to
their job.

195
00:25:54,177 --> 00:25:59,437
Flatyos, keep your eyes
on Göktuğ.

196
00:25:59,437 --> 00:26:03,636
Take his head in his
smallest mistake.

197
00:26:03,636 --> 00:26:08,336
I will behead him if his horse
stumble, Nikola.

198
00:26:08,782 --> 00:26:11,922
Don't get mad later on!

199
00:26:13,151 --> 00:26:17,911
Like you said.
Come on.

200
00:26:25,160 --> 00:26:29,160
The best thing about being an
enemy on open...

201
00:26:29,160 --> 00:26:33,160
...is not being have to hide
like rats.

202
00:26:35,116 --> 00:26:40,176
You shouldn't talk like this to
people who you...

203
00:26:40,176 --> 00:26:44,176
...use their intelligence and plans.

204
00:26:44,176 --> 00:26:48,176
You've done your part.

205
00:26:48,176 --> 00:26:52,176
Now we'll get the documents
and finish Osman.

206
00:26:52,176 --> 00:26:59,066
Meanwhile, you can play games of
war with your soldiers.

207
00:27:01,617 --> 00:27:06,597
Games of war? Do you think it's a game?

208
00:27:06,597 --> 00:27:11,867
I'll make Osman and his loved ones
bleed. You'll steal things...

209
00:27:11,867 --> 00:27:15,867
...and I will kill them.

210
00:27:15,867 --> 00:27:22,567
Then, we can't wait that, Nikola.

211
00:27:23,596 --> 00:27:27,596
Tomorrow, there will be blood.

212
00:27:28,801 --> 00:27:35,311
Osman will bleed. Either
from his head...

213
00:27:36,051 --> 00:27:42,321
...or from his heart.
Now everyone to their jobs.

214
00:27:42,863 --> 00:27:49,023
You are right. Everyone to
their own job.

215
00:28:12,298 --> 00:28:16,798
-May I enter, Osman Bey?
-Come, brother.

216
00:28:21,694 --> 00:28:26,644
Lord of Koyunhisar will go hunting
to meet you in secret tomorrow.

217
00:28:26,644 --> 00:28:28,949
-Thank you, brother.
-Thank you.

218
00:28:28,949 --> 00:28:32,269
-May I enter, my bey?
-Come, Master Davud.

219
00:28:33,635 --> 00:28:38,235
-Salam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam.

220
00:28:38,235 --> 00:28:43,205
-You summoned me, my bey.
-Sheikh Edebali is coming here today.

221
00:28:43,657 --> 00:28:48,577
-I want you to greet him.
-We will be honored, my bey.

222
00:28:48,963 --> 00:28:56,853
-Brother, his security is on you.
-Don't worry, brother.

223
00:29:05,713 --> 00:29:11,213
-May I enter, my bey.
-Come, Bala.

224
00:29:15,373 --> 00:29:20,563
-My bey, I have things to say.
-I know.

225
00:29:21,305 --> 00:29:23,085
But...

226
00:29:28,212 --> 00:29:32,212
...my answer is no.

227
00:29:35,974 --> 00:29:41,914
To give birth to a bey's son,
a bey's mother is needed.

228
00:29:44,575 --> 00:29:49,955
Find a good spouse for that woman.

229
00:29:50,767 --> 00:29:54,767
And about the mother of my heir...

230
00:29:58,349 --> 00:30:04,279
...surely, it should be a bey's daughter.

231
00:30:41,191 --> 00:30:47,101
Boran brother, Göktuğ being
banished...

232
00:30:47,106 --> 00:30:51,106
...it's not our place to
question our bey but...

233
00:30:51,106 --> 00:30:56,516
-But what? Don't question it then.
-You are right, brother.

234
00:30:57,824 --> 00:31:03,194
Our Göktuğ should survive and it's
enough. He'll be forgiven one day.

235
00:31:05,695 --> 00:31:10,325
Brother, Nikola's dogs must
be after him.

236
00:31:12,683 --> 00:31:16,683
I know, Gencebay. I know.

237
00:31:18,049 --> 00:31:22,049
Who opened Kulucahisar's gates?

238
00:31:22,835 --> 00:31:26,835
My brother Göktuğ did it.

239
00:31:27,238 --> 00:31:31,238
-He didn't die, did he?
-He didn't.

240
00:31:31,459 --> 00:31:36,689
He won't die. He'll survive.

241
00:31:39,823 --> 00:31:45,773
He won't die but he won't
return either.

242
00:31:54,420 --> 00:31:59,780
-Salam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam.

243
00:32:00,864 --> 00:32:05,494
Alps of Kayı, why are you like this?

244
00:32:23,486 --> 00:32:27,486
You are sad about Göktuğ, aren't you?

245
00:32:28,038 --> 00:32:32,748
How did our bey make that decision,
you ask.

246
00:32:32,748 --> 00:32:38,198
But you aren't the bey, you don't know.

247
00:32:38,459 --> 00:32:45,239
A man sleeps by a tree.

248
00:32:45,706 --> 00:32:52,306
The shepherd passing by sees a snake
slipping into the man's mouth.

249
00:32:52,854 --> 00:32:59,754
He hits the man on the head with
his stick. And when the man wakes up...

250
00:32:59,754 --> 00:33:04,064
...he keeps beating him. Until...

251
00:33:04,064 --> 00:33:08,064
...the snake gets out of his mouth.

252
00:33:08,064 --> 00:33:14,284
When the snake leaves, the man realizes
why he was getting beaten.

253
00:33:14,284 --> 00:33:20,164
But, ''You could tell me why you
were beating me first'' he says.

254
00:33:20,164 --> 00:33:25,784
And the shepherd says if I had
told you, you would die in fear.

255
00:33:27,145 --> 00:33:31,145
Alps, when Osman Bey hits
you with his stick...

256
00:33:31,145 --> 00:33:35,885
...don't forget this story.

257
00:33:35,885 --> 00:33:41,217
Don't make a decision until
the snake gets out.

258
00:33:46,066 --> 00:33:50,066
-Thank you, my bey.
-Thank you, my bey.

259
00:34:39,154 --> 00:34:43,154
I wouldn't think that I Turk
would save my life.

260
00:34:56,433 --> 00:35:00,053
So, you are still a Turk.

261
00:35:00,506 --> 00:35:05,366
When you drink this wine,
I will trust you.

262
00:35:10,241 --> 00:35:14,741
-Where are the spoils?
-Spoils?

263
00:35:14,870 --> 00:35:18,870
Are we thieves?

264
00:35:19,145 --> 00:35:24,135
Why did we kill all these people
if not for the spoils?

265
00:35:24,262 --> 00:35:29,422
Why is it your concern?
Do your job.

266
00:35:29,852 --> 00:35:34,722
It was needed and we've done it.

267
00:35:59,087 --> 00:36:04,787
This won't be done without
blood like Nikola says.

268
00:36:05,136 --> 00:36:11,406
Have ever seen me stepping
back, woman?

269
00:36:15,427 --> 00:36:21,317
It's a big scheme, it's dangerous.

270
00:36:22,358 --> 00:36:27,828
There will be blood. Heads will fall.

271
00:36:30,685 --> 00:36:35,615
If needed, yes.

272
00:36:36,476 --> 00:36:40,476
That's how beys fall...

273
00:36:40,476 --> 00:36:44,476
...that's how the fur changes
hands.

274
00:36:46,575 --> 00:36:50,575
If it's time for the
wolf in sheep disguise...

275
00:36:50,575 --> 00:36:54,575
...to show his teeth...

276
00:36:54,575 --> 00:37:02,785
...may Allah bless our way.
What can I say?

277
00:37:16,271 --> 00:37:21,411
Come at me! Come at me and
taste my sword!

278
00:37:28,867 --> 00:37:33,157
-Surrender!
-Ahmed Alp!

279
00:37:33,365 --> 00:37:37,365
Yiğit Alp!
I yield!

280
00:37:39,708 --> 00:38:05,748
Long live Ahmed Alp!
Long live Yiğit Alp!

281
00:38:05,748 --> 00:38:12,178
-Ahmed, get down. Osman Bey awaits me.
-A little bit more, brother Cerkutay.

282
00:38:12,636 --> 00:38:19,046
You are a man now. I can't carry you.
Get down.

283
00:38:40,323 --> 00:38:44,323
You smartened up.

284
00:38:44,580 --> 00:38:46,450
What does that mean?

285
00:38:46,450 --> 00:38:50,983
You didn't have a brain over
your shoulders before.

286
00:39:03,935 --> 00:39:09,015
I can get Ahmed Alp on my
shoulders to smarten up.

287
00:39:09,043 --> 00:39:13,043
What will you do Aygül the crazy?

288
00:39:15,403 --> 00:39:19,403
Are you so happy, Ahmed Alp?

289
00:39:20,720 --> 00:39:26,710
I forgive you this time
for making Ahmed laugh.

290
00:39:34,408 --> 00:39:39,698
Ahmed Alp, Yiğit Alp
go and play with your brothers.

291
00:40:05,537 --> 00:40:09,177
What happened, Cerkutay?
Are you all right?

292
00:40:09,177 --> 00:40:14,947
You forgave me.
Will Mohammad do the same?

293
00:40:24,767 --> 00:40:28,767
Will you stop stealing too?

294
00:40:30,345 --> 00:40:35,655
There is something else that I need to
steal. Maybe after that.

295
00:40:36,330 --> 00:40:40,330
What's that?

296
00:40:47,723 --> 00:40:51,723
-You are crazy.
-Don't you believe me?

297
00:40:52,669 --> 00:40:57,289
I will gift it to Osman Bey then.

298
00:40:57,712 --> 00:41:05,892
Fine, let's see then.

299
00:41:06,918 --> 00:41:10,048
-All right.
-All right.

300
00:41:11,064 --> 00:41:13,774
Alps!

301
00:41:14,527 --> 00:41:22,767
-I yield! I yield! I yield!
-Slowly!

302
00:41:22,767 --> 00:41:26,767
I'm running away!
I'm running away!

303
00:41:26,767 --> 00:41:30,137
Don't let him run away!

304
00:42:25,076 --> 00:42:27,846
Come on!

305
00:42:51,084 --> 00:42:56,974
Oh, my Allah!
Heal me!

306
00:43:00,367 --> 00:43:04,367
With the name of Allah!

307
00:43:06,678 --> 00:43:10,678
Oh my Allah...

308
00:43:12,952 --> 00:43:16,952
Oh my Allah...

309
00:43:21,640 --> 00:43:28,390
Oh my Allah...
Mashallah, mashallah!

310
00:43:33,743 --> 00:43:39,993
-Salam Alaikum!
-Alaikum Salam! Alaikum Salam!

311
00:43:39,993 --> 00:43:45,903
İdris Bey! İdris Bey!
It's working!

312
00:43:45,903 --> 00:43:51,173
Come on, Bamsı Bey!
Wouldn't I bring it otherwise.

313
00:43:51,339 --> 00:43:55,339
Let's take a look.

314
00:44:01,719 --> 00:44:06,989
Mashallah. Mashallah.
A little bit more and it will be fine.

315
00:44:06,989 --> 00:44:11,729
Yes, yes, Idris bey.
What are you waiting for?

316
00:44:11,916 --> 00:44:17,356
I will, I will but Bamsı Bey.
We ran out of it.

317
00:44:25,778 --> 00:44:29,778
İdris Bey, bring me another one
then.

318
00:44:29,778 --> 00:44:35,078
I will, Bamsı Bey. I will but the
roads aren't safe.

319
00:44:35,078 --> 00:44:39,078
We have to pass the Rum lands.

320
00:44:39,078 --> 00:44:43,078
Nikola's dogs are looking for
Turks to bite.

321
00:44:43,078 --> 00:44:49,008
Don't worry. I'll give you some alps.

322
00:44:49,560 --> 00:44:53,560
I thought you were hiding
your condition, Bamsı Bey.

323
00:44:53,560 --> 00:44:57,560
I don't want it to be heard.

324
00:45:04,526 --> 00:45:09,766
You are right.
You are right.

325
00:45:11,256 --> 00:45:16,546
Let's go together then, İdris Bey.

326
00:45:16,546 --> 00:45:20,546
If you come with me,
nothing can scare me, Bamsı Bey.

327
00:45:20,546 --> 00:45:24,546
-All right, but don't let anyone understand.
-Come on!

328
00:45:30,526 --> 00:45:35,836
It will be good. It will be good.

329
00:45:45,962 --> 00:45:50,362
Gündüz Bey mentioned a
profitable deal.

330
00:45:50,362 --> 00:45:54,362
I wanted to hear it from you.

331
00:45:54,362 --> 00:45:58,362
So, you aren't afraid of
the price.

332
00:45:58,362 --> 00:46:02,362
There is no price that gold
can't pay.

333
00:46:06,822 --> 00:46:11,882
-What do you want?
-Grasslands.

334
00:46:14,137 --> 00:46:21,207
-I need more grasslands.
-Have your sheep grew in number?

335
00:46:22,020 --> 00:46:26,020
Let's say that it's a preparation
for our holiday.

336
00:46:27,800 --> 00:46:33,020
You are looking for a place for
the new tribes to come.

337
00:46:33,020 --> 00:46:38,120
New tribes, new herds.

338
00:46:40,031 --> 00:46:45,321
You'll grow in power but why
should I say yes?

339
00:46:45,321 --> 00:46:49,298
I will give you 3000 gold coin.

340
00:46:49,298 --> 00:46:54,958
A good price for my animals
to eat your grass.

341
00:46:58,195 --> 00:47:05,125
Let's say that I say yes to you.
Will Nikola let me live after that?

342
00:47:05,125 --> 00:47:11,125
Then, you'll be the lord of İnegöl.
And I will support you.

343
00:47:14,031 --> 00:47:19,161
You want me to betray Nikola.

344
00:47:19,161 --> 00:47:23,148
Do you know its price?

345
00:47:23,148 --> 00:47:30,838
We both know well that there is no
price that gold can't pay.

346
00:47:36,517 --> 00:47:42,067
Well, Osman, let's see what
Nikola will say about that.

347
00:48:04,900 --> 00:48:10,290
You were going to tell it to
Nikola, huh?

348
00:48:11,877 --> 00:48:14,447
Traitor.

349
00:48:42,122 --> 00:48:47,542
Now, you look like a dog
ready to bite his owner.

350
00:49:03,589 --> 00:49:09,469
Come here after 3 days.
I'll tell you my decision.

351
00:49:42,614 --> 00:49:46,954
He is so afraid of Nikola that...

352
00:49:46,954 --> 00:49:51,616
...he plans to sell me out to
make reputation.

353
00:49:54,401 --> 00:49:58,401
He invited me to his trap.

354
00:49:59,674 --> 00:50:04,514
The lord of Koyunhisar
didn't accept. Who is next?

355
00:50:04,514 --> 00:50:10,614
We didn't come here for nothing.
He knew that we invited the tribes.

356
00:50:10,614 --> 00:50:15,494
Then, Nikola knows it.

357
00:50:15,998 --> 00:50:19,998
The lords are aware of
your intentions, my bey.

358
00:50:20,919 --> 00:50:24,599
We aren't done with Yorgo.

359
00:50:24,599 --> 00:50:28,529
My bey, what's on your mind?

360
00:50:28,713 --> 00:50:34,203
Yorgo will give us the head
of the traitor.

361
00:50:37,507 --> 00:50:41,507
We'll sow such discontent among
the lords that...

362
00:50:42,692 --> 00:50:47,382
...they won't have time
for us.

363
00:50:49,397 --> 00:50:52,467
-Abdurrahman Ghazi.
-Yes, my bey.

364
00:50:52,467 --> 00:50:59,667
Go to Yavlak Arslan. Tell him about
this meeting. We don't have time.

365
00:51:01,920 --> 00:51:08,140
Now is the time to fight.

366
00:51:09,369 --> 00:51:13,369
As you order, my bey.

367
00:52:38,858 --> 00:52:41,648
It's an ambush!

368
00:52:44,014 --> 00:52:46,484
Damn it!

369
00:52:46,884 --> 00:52:49,664
Aksu Hatun!

370
00:52:55,545 --> 00:52:59,105
Alps, charge!

371
00:53:00,748 --> 00:53:03,608
An ambush!

372
00:53:05,364 --> 00:53:09,834
Aksu Hatun! Go to the tents at once!

373
00:53:26,370 --> 00:53:31,150
Targun! Charge, alps!

374
00:53:35,607 --> 00:53:38,717
Come on!

375
00:54:24,775 --> 00:54:28,311
Gonca! Gonca!

376
00:54:35,189 --> 00:54:38,409
Go, Bala Hatun!

377
00:54:39,367 --> 00:54:43,367
Come on, come on!

378
00:54:44,764 --> 00:54:48,764
They are running away!
They are running away!

379
00:55:04,469 --> 00:55:09,759
Gonca, come on! Hang on, Gonca!

380
00:55:10,819 --> 00:55:12,989
Come on!

381
00:55:18,879 --> 00:55:21,619
Come on!

382
00:55:24,046 --> 00:55:27,456
Come on, hurry!

383
00:56:12,257 --> 00:56:17,167
-What's happening, Bamsı Bey?
-It's an ambush.

384
00:56:36,980 --> 00:56:40,020
Bamsı!

385
00:56:40,240 --> 00:56:44,240
Bamsı the mad!

386
00:56:44,340 --> 00:56:47,180
The mad lord!

387
00:56:48,965 --> 00:56:53,795
Do you know what happens to
old deer that walks alone?

388
00:56:54,179 --> 00:56:59,099
I know. I know.
Weasels like you go after it.

389
00:56:59,099 --> 00:57:03,099
Oh, old Bamsı.
Oh...

390
00:57:04,000 --> 00:57:07,350
Old.

391
00:57:14,218 --> 00:57:21,398
Nikola... Nikola...
Nikola...

392
00:57:21,985 --> 00:57:28,385
Look, Nikola. I lived enough.

393
00:57:28,385 --> 00:57:31,115
Thank Allah.

394
00:57:33,407 --> 00:57:39,597
Now, do you know why I'm happy?

395
00:57:41,846 --> 00:57:48,766
When I'm going to Allah,
I won't go empty-handed.

396
00:57:49,545 --> 00:57:54,235
Speaking of hands. They took one
of them.

397
00:57:57,640 --> 00:58:04,560
-I will get the other.
-We'll see. We'll see.

398
00:58:04,709 --> 00:58:10,789
So, old man.
Will you kneel?

399
00:58:10,832 --> 00:58:14,832
Or do we have to make you?

400
00:58:25,475 --> 00:58:30,755
İdris Bey, stand behind me.

401
00:58:33,560 --> 00:58:38,630
Nikola, if you have the courage...

402
00:58:38,630 --> 00:58:42,270
...come and get it.

403
00:59:23,906 --> 00:59:26,896
It's done.

404
00:59:32,804 --> 00:59:36,804
Pope's spy in Kayı Tribe...

405
00:59:36,804 --> 00:59:41,524
...have beaten the old plane, huh?

406
01:00:01,051 --> 01:00:04,401
İdris Bey!

407
01:00:08,448 --> 01:00:11,548
İdris Bey!

408
01:00:18,734 --> 01:00:22,194
İdris Bey!

409
01:00:49,333 --> 01:00:54,893
If you want to want me,
come after me!

410
01:01:01,862 --> 01:01:07,742
Run, Bamsı Bey, run.
So that Osman can come.

411
01:01:08,657 --> 01:01:12,057
Catch him!

412
01:01:21,621 --> 01:01:25,621
What did you do?

413
01:01:26,598 --> 01:01:30,598
Don't worry, you won't die.

414
01:01:30,598 --> 01:01:35,408
I know anatomy because
of sculpture.

415
01:01:35,408 --> 01:01:40,858
You will go to the tribe.
You know what to do, don't you?

416
01:01:41,434 --> 01:01:44,584
Get him up.

417
01:01:53,210 --> 01:01:58,170
I live you to the merciful
hands of Jesus, İdris.

418
01:01:58,170 --> 01:02:03,420
Or should I call you David? İdris or
David? David is good.

419
01:02:03,820 --> 01:02:07,820
Damn you!

420
01:02:16,753 --> 01:02:19,083
Gentlemen!

421
01:02:49,015 --> 01:02:53,465
My Allah who created
the sky and the ground!

422
01:02:53,518 --> 01:02:57,968
I greet you!
Give me the strength of Hz.Ali!

423
01:02:58,987 --> 01:03:03,707
Give me the strength of his arms...

424
01:03:03,707 --> 01:03:08,639
...and sharpness of his sword!

425
01:03:08,639 --> 01:03:13,399
You are capable of everything.

426
01:03:13,399 --> 01:03:15,709
Ya Allah!

427
01:04:37,431 --> 01:04:43,961
My Allah, please forgive me!

428
01:04:46,411 --> 01:04:50,411
Bala Hatun...

429
01:05:39,734 --> 01:05:43,304
Osman Bey!

430
01:05:48,559 --> 01:05:51,909
Aksu Hatun!

431
01:05:54,050 --> 01:05:59,500
We were attakced.
Bala Hatun...

432
01:05:59,500 --> 01:06:03,500
-What happened to Bala Hatun?
-At the turnout of Söğüt...

433
01:06:03,901 --> 01:06:07,901
...we were ambushed.
-Who?

434
01:06:07,901 --> 01:06:11,901
Targun...
Targun Hatun.

435
01:06:15,528 --> 01:06:21,148
Alps, take Aksu Hatun to the tribe.
She needs help.

436
01:06:21,148 --> 01:06:23,848
Come on, alps!

437
01:06:45,497 --> 01:06:50,927
Bala! Show yourself!

438
01:06:52,594 --> 01:06:56,094
Go on!

439
01:07:15,250 --> 01:07:24,340
You will be all right, Gonca.
Alps must be on their way.

440
01:07:25,110 --> 01:07:27,840
Be patient.

441
01:07:28,522 --> 01:07:34,882
I'm not sad, Bala. I fought
with you side by side.

442
01:07:34,943 --> 01:07:40,613
-What else can I want?
-Don't speak like this. Someone awaits you.

443
01:07:40,613 --> 01:07:44,613
Hang on a little bit longer.

444
01:07:46,219 --> 01:07:51,179
Boran...
Boran...

445
01:07:51,179 --> 01:07:56,789
Boran, yes.
Come on, let's go.

446
01:08:49,324 --> 01:08:51,744
Come on!

447
01:09:03,010 --> 01:09:06,120
Gonca...

448
01:09:07,050 --> 01:09:10,310
Come, come!

449
01:09:14,350 --> 01:09:17,480
Come on!

450
01:09:17,861 --> 01:09:21,861
Come on! Come on!

451
01:09:40,718 --> 01:09:44,268
Come, wait here.

452
01:09:48,830 --> 01:09:53,110
It's time to settle up, Bala.

453
01:09:53,110 --> 01:09:58,110
I'm here, Targun.
You'll pay for that poison.

454
01:09:58,110 --> 01:10:02,110
Stop talking and attack me!

455
01:10:02,110 --> 01:10:06,110
Leave her to me, alps!

456
01:10:43,073 --> 01:10:45,893
Attack!

457
01:10:46,971 --> 01:10:49,451
Gonca!

458
01:10:50,120 --> 01:10:52,790
Gonca!

459
01:10:54,461 --> 01:10:58,801
Hang on, Gonca!
Osman and Boran are here!

460
01:10:58,996 --> 01:11:01,656
Damn it!

461
01:11:36,910 --> 01:11:39,980
Help Gonca!

462
01:11:53,711 --> 01:11:56,861
Boran!

463
01:12:03,807 --> 01:12:07,807
Gonca!
Gonca!

464
01:12:14,229 --> 01:12:18,229
Gonca!

465
01:13:33,761 --> 01:13:37,761
You will be all right, Gonca!

466
01:13:39,021 --> 01:13:44,071
You are here...
You are here in time...

467
01:13:44,468 --> 01:13:49,428
Don't tire yourself, Gonca.
You will be all right.

468
01:13:53,804 --> 01:13:57,804
Gonca?
Gonca!

469
01:14:01,017 --> 01:14:08,087
What are you waiting for, brothers?
Hurry! Hurry!

470
01:14:09,250 --> 01:14:13,250
Gonca!

471
01:14:57,764 --> 01:15:01,064
Targun!

472
01:15:05,901 --> 01:15:09,291
Targun!

473
01:15:09,748 --> 01:15:13,748
-Come on!
-Targun!

474
01:15:14,248 --> 01:15:18,248
This isn't the end, Targun!

475
01:15:31,305 --> 01:15:38,055
-Bala, what is this?
-Targun set us a trap.

476
01:15:40,140 --> 01:15:44,140
Gonca's condition is severe, Osman.

477
01:15:55,079 --> 01:15:59,079
Where are you, Göktuğ?

478
01:16:00,092 --> 01:16:03,722
Where are you?

479
01:16:24,178 --> 01:16:29,658
-Have you figured out what happened?
-While we were waiting for the caravan...

480
01:16:29,658 --> 01:16:34,898
...Targun attacked Bala.
-What are you saying, woman?

481
01:16:36,788 --> 01:16:40,868
She couldn't get into Osman's bed...

482
01:16:40,868 --> 01:16:44,868
...so, she wants to kill Bala.

483
01:16:45,205 --> 01:16:50,685
Aksu is wounded, they brought her
here. She told what happened.

484
01:16:54,215 --> 01:16:57,515
Nikola...

485
01:16:59,770 --> 01:17:03,770
Nikola?

486
01:17:03,770 --> 01:17:07,770
Did you know about this?

487
01:17:13,092 --> 01:17:17,092
What if he brings something
else on us?

488
01:17:17,384 --> 01:17:19,634
May I enter?

489
01:17:20,616 --> 01:17:23,506
Come.

490
01:17:30,213 --> 01:17:34,213
Osman Bey brought Bala Hatun.

491
01:17:34,213 --> 01:17:38,593
-How is she?
-She is fine, thank Allah.

492
01:17:38,593 --> 01:17:43,113
But Gonca Hatun's condition is severe.

493
01:17:44,008 --> 01:17:48,008
I'm going to Osman Bey.

494
01:17:54,040 --> 01:17:57,540
Troubles come without a break.

495
01:17:57,540 --> 01:18:03,760
Lena, what's wrong? Don't you know that...

496
01:18:03,760 --> 01:18:08,400
...this won't end as long as Osman
is leading us?

497
01:18:12,621 --> 01:18:17,451
The troubles comes from Nikola,
not Osman, Hazal Hatun.

498
01:18:18,194 --> 01:18:21,854
Don't you know that?

499
01:18:24,980 --> 01:18:28,180
Lena.

500
01:18:35,716 --> 01:18:40,516
From now, Osman Bey...

501
01:18:40,813 --> 01:18:44,173
...and Bala are my family.

502
01:18:44,940 --> 01:18:48,710
Remember this, Hazal.

503
01:19:09,404 --> 01:19:13,784
-Mother Selcan!
-What's happening?

504
01:19:13,784 --> 01:19:17,784
-Hang on Gonca!
-Gonca? Boil some water!

505
01:19:17,784 --> 01:19:22,444
Mother Selcan, I need your help!
I need your help!

506
01:19:22,802 --> 01:19:26,802
Calm down, son! Is this the first
time you see someone wounded?

507
01:19:31,968 --> 01:19:35,968
It's the first time I see such
a wound, Mother Selcan.

508
01:19:36,910 --> 01:19:40,910
Wait outside now, son.
Come on!

509
01:19:42,359 --> 01:19:46,359
-Is her wound deep?
-It's deep, mother.

510
01:19:58,996 --> 01:20:04,236
-What's this?
-It was my grandmother's

511
01:20:04,532 --> 01:20:09,392
She gave it to my father and
he gave it to me.

512
01:20:21,306 --> 01:20:26,886
-If I die, that's my only heirloom.
-May Allah forbid, Boran Alp!

513
01:20:27,348 --> 01:20:32,338
Why are you talking about death now?

514
01:20:33,360 --> 01:20:37,360
Won't we die someday, Gonca Hatun?

515
01:20:45,708 --> 01:20:49,708
Take these!

516
01:20:53,066 --> 01:20:57,066
Forgive me, Bala Hatun.

517
01:21:03,086 --> 01:21:08,216
Nikola must be behind this.
There is no other explanation.

518
01:21:08,384 --> 01:21:11,084
How will we find that woman?

519
01:21:12,108 --> 01:21:17,848
-Göktuğ is with them, brother?
-You put there a spy?

520
01:21:17,848 --> 01:21:24,468
-Why didn't we hear about the raid?
-That's what I wonder.

521
01:21:24,529 --> 01:21:28,529
It seems that something
happened to Göktuğ.

522
01:21:32,441 --> 01:21:36,441
-May I enter, my bey.
-Come!

523
01:21:39,279 --> 01:21:44,239
İdris Bey! What happened to you?
Who did this?

524
01:21:44,858 --> 01:21:50,528
We were going to a healer with
Bamsı Bey, my bey.

525
01:21:51,267 --> 01:21:56,147
-Bamsı Bey?
-Nikola.

526
01:21:56,289 --> 01:22:00,289
He stopped us with his soldiers.

527
01:22:02,835 --> 01:22:08,505
They wounded me and
chased Bamsı Bey.

528
01:22:16,095 --> 01:22:20,095
Why did you go alone?

529
01:22:20,225 --> 01:22:25,545
Bamsı Bey's hand is injured, my bey.

530
01:22:25,545 --> 01:22:30,545
He didn't want anyone to know it, my bey.

531
01:23:02,537 --> 01:23:09,177
-Boran, prepare the alps. We are leaving.
-Yes, my bey.

532
01:23:26,177 --> 01:23:29,377
What happened, Osman Bey?

533
01:23:37,286 --> 01:23:41,286
Nikola is after Bamsı Bey.

534
01:23:41,507 --> 01:23:46,337
What are you saying, Osman Bey?

535
01:23:47,834 --> 01:23:52,844
Keep your eyes on him, uncle.

536
01:23:54,199 --> 01:23:58,969
I suspect that he might
be Nikola's dog.

537
01:24:42,300 --> 01:24:46,300
I lost Bala.
That was the mission Nikola gave me.

538
01:24:46,300 --> 01:24:50,420
But Osman came in time as always.

539
01:24:50,420 --> 01:24:54,420
I lost many men. It's your turn now,
Göktuğ.

540
01:24:54,420 --> 01:24:58,420
We have to raid Osman's tribe
and get the secret documents.

541
01:24:59,555 --> 01:25:05,765
How will we raid Kayı Tribe after losing
all these men?

542
01:25:05,765 --> 01:25:09,765
Osman won't be at the tribe.

543
01:25:09,765 --> 01:25:14,225
-He'll leave to save Bamsı.
-What happened to Bamsı?

544
01:25:14,225 --> 01:25:21,155
Nikola made a great plan.
We'll enter thanks to him.

545
01:25:39,997 --> 01:25:43,997
Boran. Cerkutay.

546
01:26:20,167 --> 01:26:25,317
My bey, the traces thicken
on this way.

547
01:26:25,317 --> 01:26:29,517
Both ways have traces, my bey.

548
01:26:29,517 --> 01:26:33,517
There is something
wrong with this.

549
01:26:37,898 --> 01:26:42,978
Boran, Gencebey and I will
go this way.

550
01:26:43,498 --> 01:26:48,178
-Brother, you go this way.
-All right, Osman Bey.

551
01:26:48,178 --> 01:26:54,488
-Be cautious. May Allah bless your sword.
-May Allah bless your sword.

552
01:26:54,488 --> 01:26:57,068
Come on! Come on, valiants!

553
01:27:37,854 --> 01:27:41,084
Bamsı!

554
01:27:42,934 --> 01:27:48,264
You tired us so much!
Stop being stubborn!

555
01:27:50,165 --> 01:27:55,765
This is the end of the road!
Come on, Bamsı!

556
01:27:56,481 --> 01:28:00,481
You are too stubborn!

557
01:28:00,801 --> 01:28:06,061
Look, if you surrender, we'll
wait for Osman together.

558
01:28:11,007 --> 01:28:15,007
Don't worry, before
getting the documents...

559
01:28:15,007 --> 01:28:19,887
...I won't kill you or Osman.

560
01:28:26,755 --> 01:28:31,345
The mad lord!
The mad lord!

561
01:28:32,279 --> 01:28:36,739
You don't have the power to get
those documents!

562
01:28:38,330 --> 01:28:43,740
You can't even imagine what
my power is enough to get!

563
01:28:46,410 --> 01:28:51,680
Come, come and get me!

564
01:28:56,076 --> 01:29:00,076
Catch this stubborn wolf.

565
01:29:01,468 --> 01:29:05,468
Come...
Come...

566
01:29:07,148 --> 01:29:10,458
Come...

567
01:29:39,838 --> 01:29:43,438
What will we do now?

568
01:30:07,591 --> 01:30:10,251
Bamsı...

569
01:30:29,280 --> 01:30:33,280
I must be fair.

570
01:30:33,280 --> 01:30:37,280
You are too agile for your age.

571
01:30:37,280 --> 01:30:42,790
And I like good warriors.

572
01:30:47,818 --> 01:30:51,428
He is coming, sir.

573
01:30:52,050 --> 01:30:56,050
Osman is coming.

574
01:30:57,656 --> 01:31:02,666
But you are too stubborn, Bamsı the mad.

575
01:31:02,804 --> 01:31:05,974
Too much.

576
01:31:13,124 --> 01:31:17,944
Come, Osman. Come.

577
01:31:38,839 --> 01:31:43,279
I knew that Targun would bring
bigger troubles, mother.

578
01:31:43,594 --> 01:31:47,594
It won't end before she dies.

579
01:31:48,104 --> 01:31:53,144
My pretty girl, one trouble ends
and the other begins.

580
01:31:53,144 --> 01:31:57,974
Talking about an if is no good
for anyone.

581
01:31:58,200 --> 01:32:02,200
Be cautious.

582
01:32:02,200 --> 01:32:06,200
Be cautious so that you can see
the new troubles.

583
01:32:06,200 --> 01:32:11,260
There is no one left in the tribe, mother.
Anyone but Dündar Bey.

584
01:32:11,260 --> 01:32:16,260
Oh, my girl, oh...

585
01:32:18,539 --> 01:32:22,539
Inshallah the weasels won't try to
take advantage.

586
01:32:22,539 --> 01:32:26,539
If we are left with Dündar...

587
01:32:26,539 --> 01:32:30,539
...then, may Allah protect us.

588
01:32:32,333 --> 01:32:37,433
That idiot, he was about to kill me.

589
01:32:39,347 --> 01:32:44,527
-Salam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam, Dündar Bey.

590
01:32:44,602 --> 01:32:49,242
-What's wrong, why is this honor?
-I came to tell you to get well soon.

591
01:32:49,242 --> 01:32:53,242
Mashallah, it was close.

592
01:32:53,242 --> 01:32:59,102
Yeah, it was close.
My Allah protected me.

593
01:33:05,672 --> 01:33:11,312
Was it Allah or Nikola?

594
01:33:11,656 --> 01:33:16,306
What are you saying, Dündar Bey?
Of course, it was Allah.

595
01:33:16,604 --> 01:33:20,604
You must be a good follower.

596
01:33:20,604 --> 01:33:24,604
You survived a trap that Bamsı
couldn't.

597
01:33:26,636 --> 01:33:30,866
Maybe they didn't have anything
to do with me.

598
01:33:30,866 --> 01:33:34,866
They didn't have anything to
do with you, is that so?

599
01:33:35,499 --> 01:33:41,569
Or did they use you to take Bamsı
out of the tribe?

600
01:33:44,053 --> 01:33:48,563
I'm an insignificant potter.

601
01:33:48,563 --> 01:33:52,563
What can I do to Osman Bey?

602
01:33:58,555 --> 01:34:01,525
Dündar Bey.

603
01:34:02,537 --> 01:34:07,657
You are the great Dündar Bey.

604
01:34:14,409 --> 01:34:18,409
If you betray him...

605
01:34:18,732 --> 01:34:23,522
...Osman Bey can't get up again.

606
01:34:26,543 --> 01:34:32,393
Look, the caravan you were waiting
for is here.

607
01:34:33,721 --> 01:34:38,351
I hope it will be profitable, Dündar Bey.

608
01:35:57,351 --> 01:36:02,661
-Salam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam. Welcome.

609
01:36:03,071 --> 01:36:07,071
Welcome.

610
01:36:07,730 --> 01:36:11,730
Thank you, Dündar Bey.
Our goods are from Halep...

611
01:36:11,730 --> 01:36:15,990
...Ahlat, Pasinler.
-They are all our old lands.

612
01:36:15,990 --> 01:36:19,410
They are all important for us.

613
01:36:19,410 --> 01:36:24,060
-Where should we leave the goods?
-Back side of the tribe.

614
01:36:24,060 --> 01:36:28,060
Then, you can return to Söğüt.

615
01:36:47,456 --> 01:36:51,456
Mashallah.

616
01:37:10,446 --> 01:37:15,306
Have you taken care of the alps
who stayed here?

617
01:37:15,538 --> 01:37:20,108
I re-positioned them all.

618
01:37:20,329 --> 01:37:24,329
A few guards must be left.

619
01:37:24,329 --> 01:37:28,329
Take Lena and go to Osman Bey's
tent.

620
01:37:28,329 --> 01:37:32,329
It's time. Let's take care of this...

621
01:37:32,329 --> 01:37:36,329
...without making anyone bleed.

622
01:37:36,601 --> 01:37:40,601
Don't worry, my bey.

623
01:37:40,772 --> 01:37:46,062
I just want Osman's corpse to
come to the tribe.

624
01:37:48,296 --> 01:37:53,186
That day will be our holiday.

625
01:38:42,791 --> 01:38:46,791
The tracks go this way.

626
01:40:31,133 --> 01:40:35,133
-These are fake.
-It was a trap.

627
01:40:35,133 --> 01:40:38,303
They wanted to lure us here.
Be careful!

628
01:40:38,303 --> 01:40:41,003
My bey!

629
01:40:55,943 --> 01:40:58,393
Cerkutay.

630
01:40:58,691 --> 01:41:01,391
Are you all right?

631
01:41:19,088 --> 01:41:26,078
Savcı! I brought death for
you and your son.

632
01:41:26,486 --> 01:41:31,646
Now stop hiding and face me
like a man.

633
01:41:41,134 --> 01:41:44,444
Soldiers!

634
01:41:47,369 --> 01:41:51,829
-Son, stay low!
-Don't worry, father.

635
01:41:56,404 --> 01:42:00,404
My beys...

636
01:42:01,829 --> 01:42:05,829
Give me your blessings.

637
01:42:05,829 --> 01:42:09,829
-My blessing is yours.
-Hang on, my valiant!

638
01:42:09,829 --> 01:42:13,829
Don't be sad about me...

639
01:42:14,485 --> 01:42:18,485
...if you had seen what I see now...

640
01:42:18,485 --> 01:42:22,485
...I swear you would
want to go there too.

641
01:42:24,054 --> 01:42:28,054
I bear witness that
there is no god but Allah...

642
01:42:28,054 --> 01:42:33,684
...and I bear witness that Muhammad
is the servant and Messenger of Allah.

643
01:42:36,784 --> 01:42:39,824
-Dumrul!
-Dumrul!

644
01:42:40,283 --> 01:42:45,613
Flatyos! I will kill you!

645
01:42:54,605 --> 01:42:58,605
Calm down, son!

646
01:43:06,843 --> 01:43:12,523
-Get well soon, Bala Hatun.
-Thank you, Bala Hatun.

647
01:43:13,030 --> 01:43:18,190
Get well soon, Bala Hatun.
Thank Allah that you are all right.

648
01:43:18,901 --> 01:43:22,441
Thank you, Lena Hatun.

649
01:43:22,574 --> 01:43:25,264
Welcome.

650
01:43:25,326 --> 01:43:29,836
So, it was Targun Hatun, huh?

651
01:43:29,836 --> 01:43:34,576
Yes. Let's see who else was
behind that.

652
01:43:35,640 --> 01:43:39,640
Someone will always be.

653
01:43:39,640 --> 01:43:42,790
We need to be careful about the
traitors, Bala Hatun.

654
01:43:47,787 --> 01:43:50,997
You are right.

655
01:44:03,017 --> 01:44:07,837
You've been through difficult days,
Lena Hatun.

656
01:44:08,622 --> 01:44:12,622
While I was sad because my
son would die...

657
01:44:13,665 --> 01:44:18,175
...I was nearly losing my husband.
-May Allah forbid.

658
01:44:18,773 --> 01:44:23,933
-May I enter, my lady.
-Come.

659
01:44:28,214 --> 01:44:32,214
What's wrong, Aksu Hatun.
What are you doing here?

660
01:44:36,271 --> 01:44:40,271
I have things to tell you.

661
01:44:41,352 --> 01:44:44,442
What is it about?

662
01:44:46,395 --> 01:44:50,395
I can't be ungrateful.

663
01:46:00,271 --> 01:46:04,271
Where are you, my bey?
Where are you?

664
01:46:14,643 --> 01:46:18,643
Dündar Bey.

665
01:46:18,643 --> 01:46:22,643
Let's see if you'll be pleased
to see me.

666
01:46:25,770 --> 01:46:29,770
Come on, my bey.
Come on!

667
01:46:30,052 --> 01:46:34,862
Come on! Hurry up!

668
01:46:39,617 --> 01:46:42,507
Come with me.

669
01:47:09,110 --> 01:47:13,110
You were saying something,
Aksu Hatun.

670
01:47:13,110 --> 01:47:17,490
You said that you can't be ungrateful,
why did you say that?

671
01:47:17,490 --> 01:47:21,900
-I said it because--
-Because...

672
01:47:21,900 --> 01:47:27,160
...ungratefulness is the greatest
sin. Isn't that so, daughter?

673
01:47:50,437 --> 01:47:55,857
My lady, I want you to allow me...

674
01:47:58,128 --> 01:48:02,818
...I will return to my mother.

675
01:48:03,160 --> 01:48:08,280
-You should recover first, Aksu Hatun.
-She should go. She should go.

676
01:48:08,280 --> 01:48:12,520
She should recover fully.

677
01:48:13,440 --> 01:48:18,460
The poor girl had been through
a lot.

678
01:48:18,520 --> 01:48:23,250
So, that's how the Kayı Tribe is.

679
01:48:23,250 --> 01:48:27,250
You can't know what will happen.

680
01:48:31,478 --> 01:48:38,048
-Don't worry, I'll send you with alps.
-Thank you, Dündar Bey.

681
01:48:38,048 --> 01:48:43,198
There are many troubles upon us.
We should be cautious.

682
01:48:43,198 --> 01:48:47,968
Surely, surely.
We should be cautious.

683
01:48:48,352 --> 01:48:53,882
Our best warriors are with Osman Bey.

684
01:48:53,882 --> 01:48:59,232
The heathens are known by
their treachery.

685
01:48:59,232 --> 01:49:04,562
They might attack us from all
sides.

686
01:49:06,912 --> 01:49:12,792
My nephew Gündüz and I took
many measures.

687
01:49:14,496 --> 01:49:18,496
The entrances and exits are
all held...

688
01:49:18,496 --> 01:49:22,496
...by watchers and guards.

689
01:49:22,745 --> 01:49:26,705
From now, only the friends
of the Kayı...

690
01:49:26,705 --> 01:49:30,705
...can enter our tribe.

691
01:49:50,546 --> 01:49:53,236
Bamsı Bey!

692
01:50:00,376 --> 01:50:03,816
Bamsı Bey!

693
01:50:04,659 --> 01:50:08,349
Bamsı Bey!

694
01:50:17,400 --> 01:50:21,400
Thank Allah!
Thank Allah!

695
01:50:43,269 --> 01:50:46,329
Osman.

696
01:50:47,127 --> 01:50:51,127
Look, we met again.

697
01:50:51,770 --> 01:50:56,890
-You set a trap, huh?
-Look who is talking.

698
01:50:56,890 --> 01:51:00,890
-You did the same. Many times.
-I entered your place...

699
01:51:00,890 --> 01:51:04,890
...and stabbed you in your heart.

700
01:51:14,032 --> 01:51:18,032
But you are trying to defeat me...

701
01:51:18,032 --> 01:51:22,562
...with many plots and deceptions.

702
01:51:24,221 --> 01:51:28,221
Are you worried about Bamsı?

703
01:51:29,724 --> 01:51:34,304
He fell by the tree saying
''Oh, Osman, oh... Oh...''

704
01:51:34,304 --> 01:51:38,304
He is old. That's normal.

705
01:51:43,890 --> 01:51:48,970
But don't worry. He won't die yet.

706
01:51:50,550 --> 01:51:54,550
I need you alive.

707
01:52:03,039 --> 01:52:08,579
Now, when you have the chance...

708
01:52:09,654 --> 01:52:11,904
...kill me.

709
01:52:12,947 --> 01:52:17,747
Guess who I sent to get your
father's escrows.

710
01:52:19,022 --> 01:52:23,022
Targun Hatun.

711
01:52:23,022 --> 01:52:27,022
When I'm sure that she is done...

712
01:52:27,022 --> 01:52:31,022
...I will kill you slowly.

713
01:53:10,637 --> 01:53:15,167
-What do you want?
-We have gifts for Osman Bey.

714
01:53:15,167 --> 01:53:17,537
Wait here.

715
01:53:21,134 --> 01:53:25,794
-May I enter?
-Come.

716
01:53:28,842 --> 01:53:32,842
My bey, there are gifts for Osman Bey.

717
01:53:32,842 --> 01:53:38,692
Mashallah, it's Osman Bey's caravan.
It's under Osman Bey's protection.

718
01:53:41,165 --> 01:53:45,165
Bring it. Come on.

719
01:54:55,609 --> 01:54:59,369
No one moves!

720
01:55:24,522 --> 01:55:28,522
We met again, Bala!

721
01:55:28,834 --> 01:55:32,204
Targun!

722
01:55:39,124 --> 01:55:44,194
-Göktuğ!
-Traitors...

723
01:55:51,192 --> 01:55:55,192
Ignoble!
What do you want?

724
01:56:01,453 --> 01:56:06,693
Revenge in the cruelest way.

725
01:56:13,853 --> 01:56:18,653
So, Nikola sent you, huh?

726
01:56:19,141 --> 01:56:22,581
And this exile?

727
01:56:22,581 --> 01:56:28,321
You didn't want me to be the
First Alp. So, I became your enemy.

728
01:56:31,425 --> 01:56:35,425
Let's see what will you do now.

729
01:56:36,225 --> 01:56:44,825
Traitors... Traitors don't live long,
Göktuğ. Remember that.

730
01:56:48,065 --> 01:56:52,065
That's not true, Dündar Bey.

731
01:56:52,065 --> 01:56:57,165
If it was, you wouldn't survive this far.

732
01:58:03,726 --> 01:58:08,496
I knew that you were working
with the pope's men.

733
01:58:08,496 --> 01:58:13,206
To be fair, they are very capable, Osman.

734
01:58:13,206 --> 01:58:17,206
Lower this sword.

735
01:58:17,833 --> 01:58:21,833
Let us talk.

736
01:58:21,833 --> 01:58:25,833
Don't take the pleasure of talking to
the greatest enemy I had before killing him.

737
01:58:31,365 --> 01:58:37,555
You snake! You will answer for this!
You won't get out of here alive!

738
01:58:37,555 --> 01:58:42,265
We'll leave thanks
to you.

739
01:58:42,265 --> 01:58:46,265
You wench!
Wench!

740
01:58:47,633 --> 01:58:52,873
Göktuğ, how can you do this
to Osman Bey?

741
01:58:53,469 --> 01:58:58,035
You should've asked this to Osman Bey.

742
01:58:58,035 --> 01:59:03,505
When he insulted me and kicked me,
you should've asked how could he do that.

743
01:59:05,835 --> 01:59:09,835
You couldn't do a single job.
You let Flatyos run away.

744
01:59:09,835 --> 01:59:13,835
Now are you blaming
Osman Bey for this?

745
01:59:14,602 --> 01:59:21,552
I was just in power. I was with
Osman Bey when he ran away.

746
01:59:21,760 --> 01:59:25,760
Now I'm in his tent.

747
01:59:28,803 --> 01:59:33,563
I came for revenge.

748
01:59:33,563 --> 01:59:38,603
Enough, Göktuğ.
Now it's my turn.

749
01:59:39,647 --> 01:59:43,647
Let's enter Osman Bey's private room.

750
01:59:46,448 --> 01:59:52,478
-Don't try it, don't, Targun!
-Stop me if you can.

751
01:59:54,881 --> 02:00:00,861
Don't! No! No!

752
02:00:00,861 --> 02:00:07,041
Targun, no! Don't! No!

753
02:00:18,355 --> 02:00:23,905
-Get out of there, Targun!
-Hurry, search everywhere.

754
02:00:23,905 --> 02:00:25,885
No!

755
02:00:33,172 --> 02:00:37,172
Osman Bey...
Osman Bey...

756
02:00:37,172 --> 02:00:41,552
If you had chosen me, you would
be the greatest of the beys.

757
02:00:41,971 --> 02:00:45,301
Now you'll lose everything you have.

758
02:00:45,301 --> 02:00:49,971
Traitors... Traitors...

759
02:00:53,882 --> 02:00:59,722
No! No...

760
02:02:56,122 --> 02:03:00,122
So, you will build a state, Osman Bey?

761
02:03:06,334 --> 02:03:10,774
Let's see how you'll build it now.

762
02:03:14,222 --> 02:03:19,142
Come on, take these.

763
02:03:31,825 --> 02:03:35,005
Come on.

764
02:03:45,774 --> 02:03:49,774
No... No...

765
02:03:50,022 --> 02:03:54,022
-Come on, we are leaving.
-Targun.

766
02:03:59,864 --> 02:04:05,494
Osman took his lesson.
We shouldn't give these to Nikola.

767
02:04:06,867 --> 02:04:10,867
We don't want him to get stronger.

768
02:04:11,505 --> 02:04:14,245
No.

769
02:04:15,425 --> 02:04:19,555
We'll honor the deal.

770
02:04:25,079 --> 02:04:30,919
-We should press him further.
-I said no!

771
02:04:38,194 --> 02:04:43,404
-Bala Hatun...
-Traitor!

772
02:04:46,057 --> 02:04:49,177
Bala Hatun!

773
02:05:14,725 --> 02:05:18,105
No...

774
02:05:18,826 --> 02:05:23,586
Bala Hatun. Be careful.

775
02:05:26,640 --> 02:05:30,640
Treachery is everywhere.

776
02:05:35,254 --> 02:05:38,084
No... No...

777
02:07:52,350 --> 02:07:55,950
Göktuğ!

778
02:08:02,342 --> 02:08:05,542
With the name of Allah!

779
02:08:05,542 --> 02:08:10,962
Thank Allah for returning to lands of
Ertuğrul Ghazi's son Osman Bey.

780
02:08:25,321 --> 02:08:31,551
-What's wrong, Kumral Abdal?
-My Sheikh. I came to you...

781
02:08:31,551 --> 02:08:35,551
...to learn of secrets.
I heard that...

782
02:08:35,551 --> 02:08:39,551
...Osman Bey's tribe will be raided.
Help!

783
02:09:07,716 --> 02:09:11,716
You did everything you could.

784
02:09:11,716 --> 02:09:15,716
You did everything you could
against a smarter, stronger enemy.

785
02:09:15,716 --> 02:09:20,156
But everything was for nothing.

786
02:09:20,426 --> 02:09:27,186
Your tribe is raided, your father's
escrows, the documents are taken.

787
02:09:28,436 --> 02:09:34,006
And probably there is a slaughter
going on in your tribe.

788
02:09:43,948 --> 02:09:47,948
Ignoble dog!

789
02:09:49,364 --> 02:09:53,364
Ignoble dog!

790
02:09:54,480 --> 02:10:00,800
But I'm still breathing!

791
02:10:07,933 --> 02:10:12,943
Osman! Osman!

792
02:10:13,226 --> 02:10:17,226
-Bamsı Bey!
-Bamsı Bey has awaken!

793
02:10:21,438 --> 02:10:24,298
Osman!

794
02:10:26,244 --> 02:10:30,034
We were just about to kill Osman.

795
02:10:30,034 --> 02:10:33,454
Of course, unless you kneel and beg.

796
02:10:42,259 --> 02:10:47,279
Osman, what does this dog speaks of?

797
02:10:49,063 --> 02:10:53,973
You will kneel and beg, for your
beloved ones.

798
02:10:55,812 --> 02:11:02,432
Then, you'll kiss my boots.

799
02:11:09,283 --> 02:11:15,723
Osman, today is the day we die.

800
02:11:15,793 --> 02:11:20,723
Bamsı Bey, firstly...

801
02:11:20,723 --> 02:11:23,663
...let us send them to hell.

802
02:11:23,663 --> 02:11:27,393
So, you want to die?

803
02:11:35,451 --> 02:11:41,461
Osman Bey, as you say...

804
02:11:41,713 --> 02:11:47,703
...victory belongs to those who
sharpen their weapon with their faith.

805
02:11:50,922 --> 02:11:55,692
-Victory?
-Victory!

806
02:11:55,692 --> 02:12:01,452
It belongs to those who stand together!

807
02:12:03,912 --> 02:12:09,192
-To death!
-To victory!

808
02:12:15,700 --> 02:12:44,259
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com